# Free LLM providers — generated from registry.yaml, do not edit by hand.
# Fill the keys you use, then `source` this file. Every endpoint is
# OpenAI-compatible: point any SDK/agent at the base URL next to the key.

# ── Google AI Studio (Gemini API) — base: https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/ · get a key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
export GOOGLE_AI_STUDIO_API_KEY=""
#    note: pass the key as Bearer

# ── opencode — base: https://opencode.ai/zen/v1 · get a key: https://opencode.ai/auth
export OPENCODE_API_KEY=""
#    note: these are the six ids Zen prices at zero; inside an opencode config the same id is written opencode/<model-id>. Every other id on the same base URL is metered. The catalog also still returns deepseek-v4-flash-free and laguna-s-2.1-free, which the pricing table stopped listing at zero — treat them as metered until it says otherwise

# ── OpenRouter (free models) — base: https://openrouter.ai/api/v1 · get a key: https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys
export OPENROUTER_API_KEY=""
#    note: pick models with the :free suffix; all eighteen ids carrying it are priced 0/0 and the other 354 rows are metered (read 2026-08-28). openai/gpt-oss-20b:free left that set between the 2026-08-20 and 2026-08-24 probes, leaving its metered twin behind and taking gpt-oss out of the column. Five are not coding models: openrouter/free is the Free Models Router, priced 0/0, picking whichever free model is up and the id that survives this lane rotating; nemotron-3.5-content-safety is a guardrail, ling-3.0-flash-fin finance-tuned, nemotron-3-nano-omni a perception sub-agent, and LiquidAI warns lfm-2.5-2.6b off agentic coding

# ── Groq — base: https://api.groq.com/openai/v1 · get a key: https://console.groq.com/keys
export GROQ_API_KEY=""
#    note: the ids Groq's own Free Plan Limits table names

# ── Kilo Code — base: https://api.kilo.ai/api/gateway · get a key: https://app.kilo.ai/profile
export KILO_CODE_API_KEY=""
#    note: every id listed is one the catalog marks isFree — the same catalog meters 346 more. kilo-auto/free and openrouter/free are routers and nemotron-3.5-content-safety is a guardrail classifier, so none of the three is a coding model. These ids come and go faster than the offer does, which is why they stay here and out of the Models column — meituan/longcat-2.0-free was marked isFree on the morning of 2026-09-02 and had left the catalog by a second read that evening

# ── Requesty — base: https://router.requesty.ai/v1 · get a key: https://app.requesty.ai/api-keys
export REQUESTY_API_KEY=""
#    note: the twelve ids listed are every row the catalog prices at 0, and the free plan serves those alone — ten on 2026-08-11, twelve on 2026-09-02 after nvidia/muse-glimmer-30b and nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b joined (both updated 2026-08-23). Ids here carry no :free suffix, so the price is the only thing separating them from the 686 metered rows beside them. Nine of the twelve — every NVIDIA row and both Poolside ones — are marked data_used_for_training with 30-day retention; nemotron-3.5-content-safety is a guardrail classifier rather than a coding model

# ── AIHubMix (free models) — base: https://aihubmix.com/v1 · get a key: https://aihubmix.com/token
export AIHUBMIX_API_KEY=""
#    note: every -free id the catalog prices at 0 is listed: 52 on 2026-09-02, against ten picked as the coding-relevant half of 49 on 2026-08-14 with the proprietary rows left out as likely to rotate — gpt-5.5-free, gpt-4.1-free and gemini-3.7-flash-free, the three named then, all stood nineteen days later, so the list is now the lane and the probe reports whatever joins or leaves it. Ignored on purpose: gpt-image-2-free and gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview-free generate images, and qwen3.6-plus-preview-free describes itself as "removed from the platform". `model_id` is the callable string; `model_name` beside it is a display title

# ── Z.ai (Zhipu GLM) — base: https://api.z.ai/api/paas/v4 · get a key: https://z.ai/manage-apikey/apikey-list
export ZAI_GLM_API_KEY=""
#    note: Coding-Plan keys use https://api.z.ai/api/coding/paas/v4 instead

